{"id":"beriah","name":"Beriah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:beriah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Beriah","text":"A gift, or in evil. (1.) One of Asher’s four sons, and father of Heber (Gen. 46:17). (2.) A son of Ephraim (1 Chr. 7:20-23), born after the slaughter of his brothers, and so called by his father “because it went evil with his house” at that time. (3.) A Benjamite who with his brother Shema founded Ajalon and expelled the Gittites (1 Chr. 8:13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1283","lemma":"בְּרִיעָה","xlit":"Bᵉrîyʻâh","gloss":"Beriah, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Beriah","count":8,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":9,"share":0.82},{"strong":"H1","lemma":"אָב","xlit":"ʼâb","gloss":"father, in a literal and immediate, or figurative and re","kjv":"chief, father, patrimony, principal","count":3,"share":0.27}],"verses":["Gen.46.17","Num.26.44","Num.26.45","1Chr.7.23","1Chr.7.30","1Chr.8.13","1Chr.23.10","1Chr.23.11","1Chr.7.20","1Chr.7.21","1Chr.7.22"],"related":[{"id":"ishui","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asher","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.071,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asher-the-tribe-of","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.049,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ephraim","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.03,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abdon","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"accursed","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"achbor","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adaiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"adrammelech","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id